# university academics.
*.pdf
*.ai
APRU-SCL-2027-*.md
APRU-SCL-2027-DesignBrief-v2.html
apru-icon.jpg

# Committee portrait originals as downloaded from the DOA staff directory. Same
# rule as the design art above: sources stay local, the repo ships only the
# derivatives (codebase/public/images/committee), and `npm run imagery`
# regenerates those. See committee-source/SOURCE.md for the provenance table.
committee-source/

# Notion change-board exports — client material, not source.
*ExportBlock*.zip

# Workspace root. npm hoists dependencies here now that the repo is a monorepo,
# and each app writes its build output inside itself.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel
.env*
!.env.example

# Designer drops. Source art, not deliverables, and far over GitHub 100 MB
# limit. The repo ships the derivatives built from them; keep the originals in
# shared storage. See apps/portfolio/scripts/build-imagery.mjs.
wetransfer_*.zip
*.zip

# The same drops unpacked. The 3 Sep key art is a single 231 MB SVG — an
# 11811x7874 base64 PNG with the type set in vector over it — which is over
# GitHub's 100 MB hard limit on its own. Same rule as the art above: the
# original stays in shared storage, the repo ships what `npm run imagery`
# builds from it.
wetransfer_*/

# Licensed font sources. Atlas Grotesk is a commercial face and these are the
# desktop .otf originals; the repo ships only the .woff2 the site serves.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose. Unanchored, `Fonts/` matches a directory of
# that name at any depth -- and because core.ignorecase is true on Windows that
# includes apps/client/app/fonts, which is where the .woff2 the site actually
# serves live. That would drop them from the commit and 404 every face.
/Fonts/
